      "side": 1,
      "message": "isn\u0027t it 6, not 7?\n\nany chance we can somehow make sure that we don\u0027t call it more times than we allocated the memory for?\n\ncan we have a variable for tracking offset and eventually assert that it is less than what we passed to alloca()? hopefully, the compiler can optimize it out.\n\nanother approach is to have a macro that does alloca and bn_init for the same size and call it 6 times. a bit less efficient, but lower chance to make a mistake. (and maybe the compiler can optimize out those consecutive separate alloca()s).\n\ne.g.\n#define bn_alloc_init(name, size) \\\n  uint8_t *buffer_##name \u003d alloca(size); \\\n  bn_init(\u0026name, buffer_##name, size);\n  \nor even\n#define bn_alloc_init(ptr, size) bn_init(ptr, alloca(size), size)\neven though size is calculated twice.",
