      "side": 1,
      "message": "I tried to avoid multiple alloca() calls - they are relatively expensive as each includes stack alignment. But structuring code this way I saved around 100 bytes from code like \nbn_init(\u0026R, alloca(mod_len), mod_len);\nbn_init(\u0026nR, alloca(mod_len), mod_len);\nbn_init(\u0026Q, alloca(mod_len), mod_len);\nbn_init(\u0026T, alloca(mod_len + sizeof(uint32_t)), mod_len + sizeof(uint32_t));\nbn_init(\u0026nT, alloca(mod_len + sizeof(uint32_t)), mod_len + sizeof(uint32_t));\n\nbn_init(\u0026tmp, alloca(2* mod_len + sizeof(uint32_t)), mod_len); // note it allocates more than use initially, but bn_mul_ex() will have 2X size of result.\n\n...\n\nIt is 7, because last buffer will be expanded 2x during computation. Check tmp_buf in original code - 2X of MAX.",
